# leo config for leo itself.

# The smoke test drives the real CLI through a real repository. It exists mostly
# to prove `leo check` still speaks in every combination of missing plan and
# missing manifest -- see t/smoke.sh for why that is the interesting case.
# Two suites, because they ask opposite questions. smoke drives the CLI
# through a real repository and proves it works when used correctly; negative
# proves every gate added since -- later work, numbered plans, the tools block,
# the companion documents, the session document -- actually refuses. A gate
# that opens for everyone is a decoration, and only the second suite can tell.
TEST_CMD="bash t/smoke.sh && bash t/negative.sh"
